* XOR combining-gate alternatives -- one deck per (variant, temperature, supply)
*
* Issue #282. Circuit-body TEMPLATE for make-requests.py: it carries no .lib,
* .temp, .tran, .control or .end card -- `klt sim` owns those (process corner
* via the request's corners.process, temperature via corners.temperature_c,
* analyses via analysis_steps). make-requests.py substitutes the supply value and two inlined netlist blocks:
*
*   VDD token          the supply of this deck (1.62 / 1.80 / 1.98 V)
*   DESIGN token       the text of design/ro_array_core.spice (ro_array_core,
*                      ro_ring5, ro_buf, ro_stage, ro_nand2, xor2) with the
*                      xor2 subcircuit width-scaled for the 2x variant (and
*                      verbatim for the baseline control)
*   SAMPLER token      the `.subckt sampler_dff` block of design/sampler_core.spice
*
* Four independent circuits share this deck. They have SEPARATE supply
* sources so that no one circuit's switching shows up in another's current:
*
*   1. PULSE-WIDTH BENCH (vddp) -- the nine-width fanout-1 chain of
*      sim/xor-combining-bandwidth/testbench/tb_xor2_pulse_width.spice, the
*      component measurement behind w_90. Edges, widths and windows are
*      unchanged (8 ps edges, w = 500..25 ps, 8-12 ns window).
*   2. FULL N = 4 ARRAY (vddr1..4 + vdd) -- the committed ro_array_core as in
*      sim/ro-array-core-combining/testbench/tb_ro_array_core.spice: start-up
*      by enable release at 5 ns, 60-200 ns steady-state window. Its xo drives
*      a sampler_dff data input (circuit 3).
*   3. ROOT SAMPLER LOAD (vdds) -- the same sampler_dff on xo in BOTH
*      variants, clk held low (transparent: the pass gate is on, the heaviest
*      input load the cell presents). Its supply is not part of the array
*      current.
*   4. INPUT-CAPACITANCE PROBES (vddc) -- effective switched input
*      capacitance of an xor2 pin a, an xor2 pin b (other pin at 0, output
*      driving one further xor2, i.e. fanout 1 as in a tree) and of the
*      sampler_dff D pin, by charge: C = -INTEG(i(Vramp)) / VDD over a
*      0 -> VDD ramp. These are three SEPARATE figures; the sampler load is
*      never folded into the first-stage input load.
*
* Everything is deterministic (no injected noise).

.option scale=1u

